ate-stage rare disease company focused on developing therapies that treat refractory and debilitating hypoglycemia associated with various forms of hyperinsulinism (\u201cHI\u201d). Summary of Clinical Assets Ersodetug Our lead clinical asset, ersodetug, is a potential treatment for refractory hypoglycemia caused by multiple forms of hyperinsulinism. Ersodetug is an intravenously administered human monoclonal antibody that binds to a unique site (allosteric) on the insulin receptor in insulin target tissues, such as in the liver, fat, and muscle.","filed":"2026-09-24","text_path":"text/RZLT/0001104659-26-110420-business.txt","text_chars":26000}}